wxWidgets 3.2.8: do not apply the Android GUI-port feature restrictions to
GUI-less (wxBase only) builds.

include/wx/android/chkconf.h force-disables wxUSE_INTL, wxUSE_CONFIG,
wxUSE_STDPATHS, wxUSE_DYNLIB_CLASS, wxUSE_REGEX, wxUSE_CMDLINE_PARSER, ...
for every non-Qt Android build.  Those are base-library features the
Audacity libraries use (wxTranslations/wxLocale, wxFileConfig,
wxStandardPaths, wxDynamicLibrary, ...).  The restrictions only make sense
for the (unfinished) native Android GUI port, so apply them only when
wxUSE_GUI is set; base-only builds then take their feature set from
setup.h like any other Unix build.  Features that do not build on Android
are switched off through the regular CMake wxUSE_* options instead
(native/cmake/Dependencies.cmake).

This also keeps wxBase and its users consistent: Audacity code is compiled
with __WXGTK__ (as on desktop Linux), which makes wx/chkconf.h include
wx/gtk/chkconf.h instead of wx/android/chkconf.h, so both sides must get
their wxUSE_* values from setup.h alone.
Applied by native/cmake/Dependencies.cmake (FetchContent PATCH_COMMAND).

diff --git a/include/wx/android/chkconf.h b/include/wx/android/chkconf.h
index 5ad1922..901cc25 100644
--- a/include/wx/android/chkconf.h
+++ b/include/wx/android/chkconf.h
@@ -14,8 +14,15 @@
 
 // For Qt under Android, use default configuration procedure as most features
 // should be supported (see documentation for more information)
-
-#ifndef __WXQT__
+//
+// The same holds for GUI-less (wxBase only) builds: the restrictions below
+// are about the never-finished native Android GUI port.  A base-only build
+// takes its feature set from setup.h (i.e. from the CMake wxUSE_* options),
+// exactly as on other Unix systems.  This also keeps the library and code
+// that includes these headers with a toolkit macro defined (e.g. __WXGTK__,
+// which selects a different chkconf.h) in agreement about wxUSE_* values.
+
+#if !defined(__WXQT__) && wxUSE_GUI
 
 // ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 // Disable features which don't work (yet) or don't make sense under Android.
